# ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# James Imbuido — Interactive Data Universe Portfolio
# Environment variables
#
# PHASE 0 NOTE: none of these are needed yet. The skeleton runs and
# deploys with zero environment variables. When a later phase needs a
# value, copy this file to .env.local and fill it in. .env.local is
# git-ignored and must never be committed (master plan §21).
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Supabase — Phase 5 (auth, credits, chess rewards) ──
# From Supabase Dashboard → Project Settings → API, or the Supabase MCP
# (get_project_url / get_publishable_keys).
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL="https://pzuypkxbthxevdlqynqw.supabase.co"
# Publishable key (sb_publishable_…). Safe to ship to the browser. The JS
# client accepts it in the anon-key slot; the legacy anon JWT also works.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY="your-publishable-key"
# Server-only. Never expose to the browser, never commit. NOT used by the app
# itself: privileged DB writes go through SECURITY DEFINER functions, so the
# service role key stays commented for Vercel. Set it in .env.local ONLY for
# `npm run kb:sync` (the JTB knowledge-base indexer) — never set it in Vercel.
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY="your-service-role-key"

# ── Contact form — per-IP rate limiting ──
# Server-only salt for hashing client IPs into contact_messages.ip_hash — the
# raw IP is never stored (master plan §21). Generate one with:
#   openssl rand -hex 32
# The route works without it (ip_hash is just unsalted), but set it locally and
# in Vercel so stored hashes can't be trivially matched against known IP lists.
# CONTACT_IP_SALT="your-random-hex-string"

# ── LLM provider — Phase 6 (JTB chatbot) ──
# Ollama Cloud API (https://ollama.com/api). Server-only. Must NEVER carry a
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix and must never reach the browser (master plan §21).
# Create a key at https://ollama.com/settings/keys.
OLLAMA_API_KEY="your-ollama-api-key"
# Optional: override the Ollama host for CHAT. Defaults to the cloud API; the
# client appends /api/chat to this bare host, so it must NOT already include
# /api. Set to "http://localhost:11434" to point at a local Ollama instead.
# OLLAMA_BASE_URL="https://ollama.com"
# Optional: model override. Defaults to DEFAULT_LLM_MODEL in
# lib/jtb/constants.ts — set to a smaller tag for cheaper/faster replies.
# LLM_MODEL="gpt-oss:120b"

# ── JTB retrieval (kb:sync + /api/jtb embeddings) ──
# Embeddings come from the jtb-embed Supabase Edge Function (supabase.ai
# gte-small), so both dev and production retrieval work with NO extra env
# vars: the endpoint derives from NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL, request turns
# carry the user's access token, and `npm run kb:sync` carries the service
# key (see SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY above). No local Ollama is needed for
# embeddings — OLLAMA_API_KEY is chat-only.
# Optional override: point embedTexts at a different (compatible) endpoint,
# e.g. to prove the whole-KB fallback behaves: JTB_EMBEDDING_URL=http://localhost:9
# JTB_EMBEDDING_URL=""
